esult is not retried automatically; check Health to avoid duplicates.} k_ankleRocksInstruction{In a short split stance, move the front knee gently over the toes while keeping the heel down. Switch sides halfway.} k_calfRaisesInstruction{Stand tall. Slowly lift both heels and lower with control. Use a wall for balance if needed.} k_legSwingsInstruction{Use a wall for balance. Swing one leg gently forward and back with a stable pelvis. Switch halfway.} k_lateralSwingsInstruction{Use a wall for balance. Gently swing one leg from side to side. Switch halfway.} k_reverseLungeInstruction{Alternate small backward steps and gently bend both knees. Push up through the whole front foot.} k_marchInstruction{March tall in place. Lift knees comfortably and swing opposite arms.} k_hingeInstruction{Keep knees soft, send hips back and lean forward with a long spine. Return with control.} k_squatInstruction{Stand with feet comfortably apart. Lower hips slowly back and down, then stand. Use a comfortable depth.} k_rotationInstruction{Stand tall and gently rotate the upper body left and right, keeping hips mostly still.} k_lateralLungeInstruction{Step sideways and gently bend the loaded knee. Return to centre and switch.} k_gluteBridgeInstruction{Lie on your back with knees bent. Lift hips without arching the lower back, then lower.} k_birdDogInstruction{On hands and knees, slowly extend the opposite arm and leg. Keep the back steady, then switch.} k_shoulderCirclesInstruction{Relax your arms and make small, slow shoulder circles backwards and forwards.} k_armCirclesInstruction{Raise arms comfortably to the sides and make small circles. Increase range only if pain-free.} k_wallSlidesInstruction{Stand with your back lightly against a wall. Slide arms up and down without arching your back.} k_scapularPushupInstruction{On hands and knees with straight arms, gently move the shoulder blades together and apart.} k_calfStretchInstruction{Place hands on a wall in a split stance. Keep the back